Biographical Sketch
Markus Amann obtained his Degree in Electrical Engineering at the Technical University of Vienna, Austria, in 1984, and a Ph.D. in Economics from the University of Karlsruhe, Germany, in 1991.
He was a Research Scholar at the International Institute for Applied Systems Analysis (IIASA) from 1985–1991, and since 1991 he has been the Leader of the Transboundary Air Pollution Project.